#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kcontrolcenter; provides users with a single integrated interface from "
"which to manage a wide variety of system and desktop settings and "
"preferences. &kcontrolcenter; can be started by selecting "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>K Menu</guimenu><guimenuitem>&kcontrolcenter;</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &knetworkconf; package was developed to enable users to manage TCP/IP "
"networking settings in the same way they manage other system settings from "
"&kcontrolcenter;. Tasks enabled by &knetworkconf; provide users with a "
"simple interface from which to perform the following tasks:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Apply IP addresses to interfaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Apply netmasks to interfaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start and stop interface activities"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Routing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Host- and Domain Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Resolving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Manage known hosts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once installed a new module called <guimenuitem>Network Settings</"
"guimenuitem> is displayed in the &kcontrolcenter;. To start the "
"<application>Network Settings</application> (&knetworkconf;) module select "
"<menuchoice> <guimenuitem>&kcontrolcenter;</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Internet &amp; Network</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Network "
"Settings</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> in the &kmenu;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "&knetworkconf; in user mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is important to understand that &knetworkconf; cannot install networking "
"hardware. As such physical devices and their drivers must be properly "
"installed and configured in order for &knetworkconf; to display the device "
"and enable management of networking properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In most cases drivers for networking hardware and other devices are "
"installed and configured while installing &Linux;. If you add networking "
"hardware after installation, you will have to define the drivers to be "
"loaded by editing one of the following files depending on your kernel "
"version:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Linux; Kernel 2.4 and lower"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "/etc/modules.conf"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Linux; Kernel 2.6 and higher"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "/etc/modprobe.conf"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Network Settings Module"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <application>Network Settings</application> module is loaded when the "
"<guibutton>Network Settings</guibutton> option is selected in the "
"&kcontrolcenter; index. When started the <application>Network Settings</"
"application> module attempts to automatically detect the platform running on "
"the system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detecting the platform"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the platform is not a recognized you will be prompted to manually "
"select the platform. Select a platform from the list that most closely "
"corresponds to your distro and its release. Check the <guibutton>Don't ask "
"again</guibutton> option to make this choice permanent. Next time "
"<guibutton>Network Settings</guibutton> is started the system will "
"automatically default to the selected platform option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To manage the system network settings you must enter <quote>administrator "
"mode.</quote> Prior to this all options will be <quote>grayed,</quote> "
"meaning you can only navigate the interface and view properties. Editing is "
"disabled. To enter <quote>administrator mode</quote> click the "
"<guibutton>Administrator Mode</guibutton> button located bottom left of the "
"module. Enter your password when prompted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&knetworkconf; in administrator mode</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&knetworkconf; in administrator mode</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once in <quote>administrator mode</quote> all the modules functionality is "
"enable. Functionality is organized into three tabs:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing Network Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Network Interfaces</guibutton> tab is used to manage the "
"network communications devices installed on the system. All available "
"networking devices are listed. From the <guibutton>Network Interfaces</"
"guibutton> tab the following tasks can be accomplished:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &knetworkconf; interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "For each network device the following properties can be viewed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface"
msgstr "Interfaç"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shows the name of the network interfaces. For example, eth0, eth1, wlan0."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "IP Address"
msgstr "Adreça IP"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows the currently assigned IP address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "Protocol"
msgstr "Protocòl"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows the boot protocol."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "State"
msgstr "Estat"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows the current state (up or down)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comment"
msgstr "Comentari"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows the (freely assignable) comment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring a Networking Device"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The properties of listed network devices can be configured by selecting the "
"required device from the list then <action>clicking</action> the "
"<guibutton>Configure Interface...</guibutton> button to display the "
"<interface>Configure Device</interface> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Configuring a networking device</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Configuring a networking device</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default only basic TCP/IP settings are available. Click the "
"<guibutton>Advanced Settings</guibutton> button to expand the dialog to "
"include advanced properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:353 index.docbook:455 index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced device configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "Complete the dialog values are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr "Automatic"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the <guibutton>Automatic</guibutton> radio button when the TCP/IP "
"settings are obtained from a DHCP server or BOOTP server node. In automatic "
"mode the TCP/IP settings for the system are configured when the system "
"services are started. The DHCP or BOOTP server sends all the required TCP/IP "
"information each time the system is started, there is no need to configure "
"any other settings. Use the drop-list to select <option>DHCP</option> or "
"<option>BOOTP</option> according to your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Manual"
msgstr "Manual"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the <guibutton>Manual</guibutton> radio button when you do not use "
"DHCP or BOOTP for TCP/IP configuration. In the <guibutton>IP address</"
"guibutton> field enter the TCP/IP address of the host. In the "
"<guibutton>Netmask</guibutton> field enter the subnetwork address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "Activate when the computer starts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked this option will cause the system to initialize this network "
"interface while the system is booting. If you do not want the device "
"initialized leave this option unchecked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descripcion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter a descriptive name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid "Broadcast"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the <quote>broadcast address</quote> used to communicate with all "
"hosts on the subnetwork."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The values entered in this dialog will be displayed as the properties of the "
"device in the device list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make certain that the IP-address entered is not already in use on the "
"network. Entering an IP-address that is already on the network will result "
"in a TCP/IP conflict. Use <application>ping</application> from &konsole; to "
"check if the address you want to enter is in use or not. If you are not sure "
"how to complete this dialog, consult your network administrator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enabling a Network Device"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Network devices may be enabled or disabled depending on system requirements. "
"To enable a disabled network device select the device from the list then "
"click <guibutton>Enable Interface</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disabling Network Devices"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Network devices may be enabled or disabled depending on system requirements. "
"To disable an enabled network device select the device from the list then "
"click <guibutton>Disable Interface</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing System Routing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Routes</guibutton> tab enables management of the system "
"routing configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default Gateway"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This specifies the IP address of the host on the local subnetwork that "
"provides the physical connection to remote networks, and is used by default "
"when TCP/IP needs to communicate with computers on other subnetworks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select a device from the drop list to edit the <guibutton>Default Gateway</"
"guibutton> value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your computer offers more than one network interface, select the "
"interface connected to network on which the gateway computer resides."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing DNS Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Domain Name System</guibutton> tab enables management of the "
"system DNS configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "Host name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "The name by which the host will be known on the subnetwork."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "Domain name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid "The network domain in which the host resides."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid "Domain Name Servers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A list of DNS servers in order of preference (see <xref linkend=\"manage-dns"
"\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "Static Hosts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A list of known hosts on the subnetwork system (see <xref linkend=\"manage-"
"hosts\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:525
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing DNS Servers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A computer running DNS matches up a fully qualified domain with a proper IP "
"address. This is necessary because computers only understand the IP "
"addresses. When a computer requests http://www.somedomain.com the DNS "
"resolves this name to an IP-address such as 123.45.678.90."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Domain Name Servers</guilabel> part of the <guibutton>Domain "
"Name System</guibutton> tab enables easy management of the list. Server "
"properties can be added, removed and edited. DNS records can be arranged in "
"order of preference by selecting a record and promoting or demoting the "
"record in the list using the <guibutton>Move Up</guibutton> or "
"<guibutton>Move Down</guibutton> buttons as required."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding a DNS server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From the <guilabel>Domain Name Servers</guilabel> group click the "
"<guibutton>Add...</guibutton> button. The <guilabel>Add New DNS Server</"
"guilabel> dialog is displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the IP-address of the DNS server then click <guibutton>Add</"
"guibutton>. The record is added to the DNS list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Editing a DNS server record</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From the <guilabel>Domain Name Servers</guilabel> group select a DNS record "
"then click the <guibutton>Edit...</guibutton> button. The <guilabel>Edit "
"Server</guilabel> dialog is displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Editing a DNS server record</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Modify the IP-address then click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. The record is "
"updated to the DNS list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing Static (Known) Hosts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Static Hosts</guilabel> list describes a number of hostname-to-"
"address mappings for the TCP/IP subsystem. It is mostly used at boot time, "
"when no name servers are running. On small, closed network systems, it can "
"be used instead of Domain Name Servers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, the <guilabel>Static Hosts</guilabel> list contains some records "
"describing the &apos;localhost&apos; and a handful of special records for "
"hosts that support IPv6. This still-experimental version of IP is destined "
"to replace version 4."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding Static Hosts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>Add...</guibutton> button. The <guilabel>Add New Static "
"Host</guilabel> dialog is displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the IP-address of the known host then click <guibutton>Add...</"
"guibutton>. The <guilabel>Add New Alias</guilabel> dialog is displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the name of the known host then click the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> "
"button. If the known host has multiple aliases click the <guibutton>Add</"
"guibutton> button again and enter another alias."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When finished click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to update the Static Hosts "
"list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing Static Hosts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:644
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select a static host record from the list, then click the <guibutton>Edit..."
"</guibutton> button. The <guilabel>Edit Static Host</guilabel> dialog is "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:659
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Perform any of the following tasks, then click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to "
"update the Static Hosts list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the IP-address, enter a new IP-address, then click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid "To add a new alias, click the <guibutton>Add...</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change an alias value, select the alias record, then click "
"<guibutton>Edit...</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an alias, select an alias record then click <guibutton>Remove</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid "Applying Changes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changes made via the <application>Network Settings</application> module are "
"not automatically applied to the system environment. To apply the changes "
"made, start &konsole; and execute the following command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>/etc/init.d/networking</command> restart</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Installacion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:703
#, no-c-format
msgid "You need &kde; 3.x and QT 3.x installed to use knetwork-conf."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid "knetwork-conf can be used with the following platforms:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:708
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kubuntu;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:711
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Conectiva</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Debian</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:717
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Fedora Core</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>FreeBSD</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:723
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Gentoo</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>&Mandrake;</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>PLD</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:732
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>OpenNA</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>&RedHat;</para>"
msgstr ""

